+## The ask in the first-time rating sheet (rule 1605)
+
+After a first rating, "When did you watch it?" (the sheet from Picks and the hold menu, and the film page's first ask under its stars) carries the same ask as Your rating, from the same component (`RatingAsk`): "We said 82%. Called it." from the save's own guess (never a star guess; nothing where no match showed), then "What did you like?" / "What did we miss?" / "What didn't work?" with "Optional", a hairline above and the film's chips, saved to rating_reasons as everywhere else. Signed-in accounts only. It asks once: the take step after it keeps its headline and box without chips. Log a watch, the onboarding taste deck, the rate-films grids and "How was it?" are unchanged.
+
 ## Pitch with nothing to show (rule 1599)
 
 When a pitch's own facts leave no film (not "seen them all", a thin service, a watchlist, rewatch, award or in-theaters pitch, which keep their own lines), the answer carries `emptyHelp` (lib/recut-rank.ts `emptyHelp`): the hard chip that rules out the most (its × chip outlined in the one red), "Nothing fits all of that." in Bodoni, "<chip> rules out the most. Without it, N films fit." and "Drop <chip>" as the one cream button; under "Or try" two nearby asks that have films, each the pitch with one or two chips off, said as a short ask (`askLine`: "A Korean musical comedy on Netflix"), a tap takes those chips off for free as a chip's × does; then "Browse instead ›", which closes Pitch and opens Browse with the pitch's genres, decade and length on. Your cut's header is hidden while it shows; the notes row stays. Web `PitchEmpty` (Recut.tsx), iPhone `pitchEmpty` (Recut.swift).
